# PLAT-036: MANIFEST.in for sdist / PyInstaller data inclusion
include LICENSE
include README.md
include SECURITY.md
include CHANGELOG.md
include CONTRIBUTING.md
include FEATURES.md
include pyproject.toml

# Server Python modules
recursive-include voice_typer/server *.py

# WR-19: include voice_typer/server/native/ data files (binaries.json +
# linux-key-listener, linux-key-listener.c, macos-key-listener.swift,
# windows-key-listener.c). Without these, `pip install voice-typer` from
# sdist leaves native_hotkeys/binary_path.py and spec_parser.py unable
# to locate or compile the listener at runtime.
recursive-include voice_typer/server/native *

# WR-19: include the bundled Silero VAD TorchScript model
# (voice_typer/server/silero_vad.jit, ~1.8 MB). Loaded at runtime by
# voice_typer/server/vad.py:38. Without this, `pip install voice-typer`
# from sdist leaves VAD raising RuntimeError at first dictation.
# (Frozen builds via voice-typer.spec:107 already include this file
# explicitly; this entry closes the sdist gap.)
#
# Phase 1a (companion §2.5): the .jit is RETAINED until Phase 1c
# (total torch removal) — Parakeet + Qwen still use torch between 1a
# and 1c, and the Nuitka flag --module-parameter=torch-disable-jit=no
# (C-CI-8 / NU-106) protects the bundle while torch is shipped. Do NOT
# delete the .jit or this MANIFEST entry at Phase 1a.
include voice_typer/server/silero_vad.jit

# Phase 1a (companion §2.3.1): include the bundled Silero VAD ONNX
# model — the new ORT backend's primary model file, loaded by
# voice_typer/server/vad.py via onnxruntime.InferenceSession. Without
# this, `pip install voice-typer` from sdist leaves VAD raising
# FileNotFoundError at first dictation. (Frozen builds via
# voice-typer.spec and the build_sidecar_*.sh Nuitka invocations
# must also include this file — see companion §2.3.1 for the full
# packaging checklist; those edits are out of this slice's scope.)
include voice_typer/server/silero_vad.onnx

# The bundled GTCRN noise-suppression streaming model
# (voice_typer/server/gtcrn_simple.onnx, ~0.5 MB, official streaming
# export). Loaded at runtime by
# voice_typer/server/audio_filters/gtcrn_backend.py via
# onnxruntime.InferenceSession for the "gtcrn" noise-suppression method
# (selected by the noisy_room preset). Without this, `pip install
# voice-typer` from sdist leaves the suppressor degrading to RNNoise
# with an is_degraded warning. Zero network egress — the model ships
# beside silero_vad.onnx and the frozen bundle's
# --include-package-data=voice_typer.server picks it up (C-CI-9).
# 2026-08-25 local verification: model binary absent from this tree — the cloud patch exports text-only diffs and cannot carry binaries (expected size 535190 bytes, MIT streaming export). Restored via review entry GA-1; re-enable this line when the asset lands.
# 2026-09-07: asset delivered (GA-1) — official export fetched from the upstream
# repo (Xiaobin-Rong/gtcrn, stream/onnx_models/gtcrn_simple.onnx), size verified
# 535190 bytes, MIT license, I/O contract verified against gtcrn_backend.py
# (mix[1,257,1,2] in, enh + 3 recurrent caches out). Line re-enabled.
include voice_typer/server/gtcrn_simple.onnx

# Corrections data + reserved-hotkey table + model integrity hashes.
# All three JSON files are read by voice_typer/server/ modules at
# runtime (config_validators._load_reserved_data, security.verify_model_integrity,
# text_cleanup.configure_corrections) and must be present in both the
# sdist and the PyInstaller bundle (see scripts/build/voice-typer.spec).
include voice_typer/server/corrections.json
include voice_typer/server/hotkey_reserved.json
include voice_typer/server/model_hashes.json

# WR-19: removed three dead lines that referenced voice_typer/server/assets/
# (the directory does not exist on disk — verified via `ls
# voice_typer/server/assets/`). The previous `recursive-include
# voice_typer/server/assets *` + two `include voice_typer/server/assets/*.png`
# / `*.ico` lines silently matched nothing.
# WR-19: also removed `recursive-include voice_typer/client/build *` —
# the electron-vite build output directory is `voice_typer/client/out/`
# (not `build/`), and the renderer is built separately by CI / Tauri,
# not shipped with the Python sdist.
